--- body ---
## Context
Ticket 0105 left the `Erg` struct storing header values in a
`map[string][]string` bag with string-keyed lookups. Replace with typed
fields matching the spec's 6-header closed set; drop the accessor
methods that exist only as map wrappers.

## Current shape (verbatim, erg.go:11-24)
```go
type Erg struct {
    Path     string
    headers  map[string][]string
    LogLines []string
    Body     string
    HasMagic bool
    LogSepCount  int
    BodySepCount int
    ClosedInLog  bool
    ClosedInBody bool
}
```

## Proposed shape
`ParseDiagnostics` is a sibling struct returned alongside `Erg`. In 0117
it is replaced in-place by `[]ParseError`; the two-return-value signature
stays across both refactors.

```go
// Line is a single-line string: no embedded newlines.
// Enforced by the parser invariant (header values read up to LF).
type Line = string

// Erg is the schema-literal projection of a %erg v1 ticket.
type Erg struct {
    Path     Line
    HasMagic bool

    // v1 headers — typed fields populated from first occurrence
    Title      Line   // required, non-empty (spec tightened — see below)
    Created    Line   // required, non-empty
    Author     Line   // required, non-empty
    Closed     Line   // optional; non-empty when present
    BlockedBys []Line // possibly empty; one entry per `Blocked-by:` line
    Tags       []Line // possibly empty; one entry per `Tag:` line (after 0106)

    LogLines []Line   // one structured event per entry
    Body     string   // multiline
}

// ParseDiagnostics carries parser observations the validator consumes.
// In 0117 (parse+validate merge) this struct is replaced in-place by
// []ParseError; until then, validate.go walks these fields.
type ParseDiagnostics struct {
    Unknown            []Line  // unknown header keys seen
    RepeatedSingletons []Line  // singleton keys seen more than once
    ClosedEmpty        bool    // ANY `Closed:` line seen with empty value
    ClosedInLog        bool
    ClosedInBody       bool
    HasLogSep          bool    // `--- log ---` was seen at least once
    HasBodySep         bool    // `--- body ---` was seen at least once
}

func parseErg(path string) (Erg, ParseDiagnostics)
```

## Parser invariants (pinned)
The implementer must preserve these semantics; they are easy to break
when moving from the map bag to typed fields.

- **Tag trimming**: today's `Tag()` accessor (renamed from `Tags()` in
  PR #122) trims values and drops empty entries (erg.go:88-101). Parser
  must apply the same when appending to the `Tags` field — trim, skip
  empty after trim.
- **`HasLogSep` / `HasBodySep`**: set to true on **any** sighting of
  the separator literal, regardless of whether the parser transitions
  sections on that sighting. Set unconditionally; do not gate behind
  the first-occurrence transition.
- **`ClosedEmpty`**: set to true if **any** `Closed:` line appears with
  an empty (post-trim) value, not only the first occurrence. A
  `Closed: ok` followed by `Closed: ` must still produce the empty-value
  error from validator rule 4. (The repeated-singleton rule also fires
  via `RepeatedSingletons`, but the empty-value signal is independent.)
- **`Closed` field stores the first non-empty value** (matching today's
  `Closed()` behavior). If only empty `Closed:` lines appear,
  `Closed = ""` and `ClosedEmpty = true`.

## Spec tightening (required headers)
Update `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`: required headers (`Title`, `Created`,
`Author`) must have a non-empty value. Today the validator passes
`Title: ` (key present, value empty) because rule 2 only checks key
presence. After this refactor, empty required headers fail validation.

## Spec clarification (line-string cardinality)
Update `tickets/spec-erg-v1.md`:
- §Headers (table): add prose immediately after the table noting that
  **all header values are line-strings — single line, no embedded
  newlines**. Multiline content belongs in the body section.
- §Headers Type column: distinguish `line` (single line) from freeform
  string. Today every header is typed `string` regardless of cardinality.
- §Log already says "Each line records one event" — no change needed
  there.

## Spec relaxation (separator duplicates)
Validator rule 11 (validate.go) rejects duplicate `--- log ---` /
`--- body ---` separators. Relax to first-occurrence; the parser
already transitions sections that way (erg.go:248-261). Legitimate
bodies quote the format literals.

Change:
- Drop the "appears N times" branch of rule 11; keep only "missing".
- §Structure: "Both separators are required" → "The first
  `--- log ---` and the first `--- body ---` (in order) are the section
  separators. Subsequent occurrences are body text."
- `const helpValidate` (validate.go) updated to match.
- Replace `LogSepCount`/`BodySepCount` with `HasLogSep`/`HasBodySep`
  bools in `ParseDiagnostics`.

Pre-existing wart (not addressed here): `isClosedHeaderLine`
(erg.go:307-310) flags `Closed:` at column 0 anywhere in the body.
Worth its own ticket if it bites.

## Accessor methods go away
Trivial accessors are deleted; call sites read fields directly. Two
methods with real logic survive:
- `IsClosed()` — path test OR non-empty `Closed` field (renamed from
  `Closed()` to avoid shadowing the new `Closed` field).
- `BlockedByRefs()` — parses every raw ref string.

| Today               | After                                          |
|---------------------|------------------------------------------------|
| `t.Title()`         | `t.Title` (direct read)                        |
| `t.Created()`       | `t.Created`                                    |
| `t.Author()`        | `t.Author`                                     |
| `t.ClosedHeader()`  | `t.Closed != ""`                               |
| `t.BlockedBy()`     | `t.BlockedBys`                                 |
| `t.Tag()`           | `t.Tags`                                       |
| `t.Closed()`        | `t.IsClosed()` (renamed; same logic)           |
| `t.BlockedByRefs()` | unchanged method, iterates `t.BlockedBys`      |

## Call-site impact
21 accessor call sites across 6 files. After this refactor:
- archive.go: `Closed()` → `IsClosed()`; `BlockedByRefs()` stays; `ClosedHeader()` → `t.Closed != ""`
- check.go:   `ClosedHeader()` → `t.Closed != ""`; `Closed()` ×2 → `IsClosed()`; `BlockedByRefs()` stays
- close.go:   `Closed()` ×2 → `IsClosed()`; `BlockedBy()` → `t.BlockedBys`
- ready.go:   `Closed()` ×2 → `IsClosed()`; `Tag()` → `t.Tags`; `BlockedByRefs()` stays; `Title()` → `t.Title`
- validate.go: `Created()` → `t.Created`; `BlockedByRefs()` ×2 stays; the 4 direct `t.headers[...]` accesses switch to typed fields on `Erg` and bools on `ParseDiagnostics`

## Dead code retirement
After the refactor, these constants in `ergspecv1.go` (not validate.go —
validate.go only uses them) become unreachable and must be removed in
the same PR:
- `RequiredHeaders` at ergspecv1.go:18 (was driving rule 2 via map lookup)
- `SingletonHeaders` at ergspecv1.go:26-28 (was driving rule 3 singleton)
- `ValidHeaders` at ergspecv1.go:37-40 (was driving rule 3 unknown-header)
- `ValidTagValues` stays — backs the Tag closed-set enumeration rule
  which still applies.

## Test impact
- erg_test.go: parser tests construct `Erg` literals — update to new
  shape. Parser tests now also assert `ParseDiagnostics` content where
  relevant.
- validate_test.go: rule 2 fixtures adjusted for empty-required-header
  tightening; add a positive test for it. Add a `Closed:` duplicate
  empty-value test (`Closed: x\nClosed: ` must trigger both repeated-
  singleton AND empty-value errors).
- New fixture: a body containing `--- log ---` and `--- body ---` as
  text. Assertions:
  (a) validator accepts the file;
  (b) `erg.Body` preserves the literal lines verbatim (no silent loss);
  (c) `ParseDiagnostics.HasLogSep` and `.HasBodySep` are true.

## Out of scope
- Parser/validator merge into one pass — ticket 0117.
- Type tightening (`BlockedBys []Ref`, `Created time.Time`) — ticket 0118.
- `Tags:` → `Tag:` header rename — ticket 0106. The Go field stays
  `Tags []Line` (idiomatic plural slice) regardless of merge order.
- Function-level splits in `parseErg`.

## Endpoint shape (after 0117 and 0118)
```go
type Erg struct {
    Path     Line
    HasMagic bool

    Title      Line       // required, non-empty
    Created    time.Time  // parsed at parse time
    Author     Line       // required, non-empty
    Closed     Line       // optional; non-empty when present
    BlockedBys []Ref      // each ref parsed at parse time
    Tags       []Line

    LogLines []Line
    Body     string
}

func parseErg(path string) (Erg, []ParseError)
```

`ParseDiagnostics` and `BlockedByRefs()` vanish; only `IsClosed()`
survives.

## Dependencies
- 0115 landed (PR #120) — Ref is in `ref.go`; this ticket touches only
  the Erg portion of erg.go.
- 0114 landed (PR #121) — validator help text lives in
  `const helpValidate` (validate.go). Edit there, not in `helptext.go`.
- 0106 (PR #122) sequencing: plan is for #122 to merge first. If 0106
  merges first, the accessor-elimination table's "Today" column shows
  `t.Tag()` (post-#122) instead of `t.Tags()`. Field name `Tags []Line`
  is unaffected by order.

## Exit criteria
- `Erg` struct contains exactly the schema-pure fields: `Path`,
  `HasMagic`, `Title`, `Created`, `Author`, `Closed`, `BlockedBys`,
  `Tags`, `LogLines`, `Body`. Nothing else.
- `ParseDiagnostics` carries the trace fields; `parseErg` returns
  `(Erg, ParseDiagnostics)`.
- All trivial accessor methods are removed; only `IsClosed()` (renamed
  from `Closed()`) and `BlockedByRefs()` remain.
- `type Line = string` alias declared; line-string fields use `Line`,
  multiline `Body` stays `string`.
- Dead constants removed: `RequiredHeaders`, `SingletonHeaders`,
  `ValidHeaders` in ergspecv1.go.
- Spec updates land in the same PR:
  - §Headers: line-string cardinality stated; Type column distinguishes
    line vs. freeform.
  - §Structure: separator-duplicates relaxed to first-occurrence.
  - §Headers + helpText: required headers (Title, Created, Author) must
    be non-empty.
- `make test` passes; new tests assert:
  (a) empty required header is rejected;
  (b) body containing `--- log ---`/`--- body ---` literals is accepted
      AND `erg.Body` preserves them verbatim;
  (c) `Closed: x\nClosed: ` triggers both repeated-singleton and
      empty-value errors.
